{
 "id": "2025-zhu-fitness",
 "name": "Fitness Trail Landscapes: Layout Choice and SD Ratings",
 "description": "Faithful replication with the paper's own stimuli (Part 1) and method replication (Part 2): participants first choose which fitness-trail environment combinations they prefer (plant-plant, plant-water, terrain-water, plant-public service facilities, plant-terrain), each shown as the real photo and block-model diagram printed in Table 2 of Zhu, Chen, Wang & Hu (2025), Frontiers in Psychology 16: 1595451 (CC BY 4.0). They then browse the five trail photos and rate each on the paper's three 7-point semantic-differential items: sense of security, pleasure and experience (Table 5). Differences from the original study: (1) the paper's SD ratings used 80 of the authors' own photos (40 plant-plant, 40 plant-water, 10 per participant, after browsing 15 typical images), which are not published, so Part 2 uses the five Table 2 photos instead and cannot reproduce the image-indicator regressions; (2) the paper does not say how many combinations each respondent could pick (240 picks from 87 respondents), so any number may be chosen; (3) option and photo order are random; (4) the trail-use frequency question is our own wording, replacing the paper's recruitment of trail users on site; age and gender are added.",
 "author": "Zhu, Chen, Wang & Hu",
